<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ivan I of Moscow</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1288–<a href="/years/1340">1340</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Ivan Kalita, Ivan I Kalita</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ivan I Danilovich, called Kalita ('moneybag'), was Prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> from 1325 and Grand Prince of Vladimir from 1328 until his death in 1340. He helped the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> crush the Tver rising of 1327, gained the right to collect the Mongol tribute from other princes, and had the Metropolitan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a> and all Rus' settle in Moscow, laying the foundations of Moscow's rise.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ivan-i-of-moscow.jpg" alt="Ivan I of Moscow" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Collective · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ivan_Kalita.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
